WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:15.000
Start with database overload: 500 requests/s and two connections.
These are recorded Python/SimPy snapshots.

00:15.000 --> 00:30.000
Inspect the database queue, utilization and failed requests.
Use measured evidence to form a bottleneck hypothesis.

00:30.000 --> 00:45.000
Add a read cache. Keep workload, seed and database capacity fixed.
Inspect the candidate's measured results.

00:45.000 --> 01:00.000
Compare throughput, latency, success rate and illustrative cost.
These results do not establish production capacity.

01:00.000 --> 01:15.000
Share a read-only snapshot of the configuration and results.
Recipients can inspect it without signing in.
